",8,-8,1,"nit: Looks like we could make this `const raw_ptr<const ash::ShelfModel>`"],["1dfb185c_fb1cd75e",8,-7,1,"nit: This part of the comment can probably be dropped (not super necessary)"],["81037f50_8aa45d53",8,-7,1,"nit: Could we add a comment indicating that this is done as Browser iterator APIs do not support creation order (this is not provided by the android platform)."],["dbd39f37_ced9fc06",8,-7,1,"nit: Could we update this comment to indicate this returns all available browsers maintained in an order that remains consistent between calls?"],["1fe6bf30_d5331be7",11,-3,1,"Test: How it was tested? Would it be possible to add unit test?"],["c8efee20_66760725",8,-3,1,"nit: Android? Also why Android is important here?"]],0,19],[7172319,20412,122,2.344,1.853,[[1,0.823,17,101],[2,0.177,3,21]],[["6d37519c_8f80681c",106,-1,1,"nit: In this iterator `browser` will always be defined so we can skip the `browser` check here."]],0,20],[7185279,20424,92,2.344,1.853,[[0,0.68,3,63],[11,0.289,3,27],[1,0.031,18,2]],[["c49e9e9e_9343feeb",104,3,0,"since this CL landed, this test has been super flaky on all platforms, see https://luci-milo.appspot.com/ui/test/chromium/%3A%2F%2Fchrome%2Ftest%5C%3Abrowser_tests!gtest%3A%3ABrowserCloseManagerBrowse…"]],0,21],[7094048,20426,68,2.344,1.853,[[32,1]],[["",107,-34,1],["",107,-34,1],["",107,-34,1],["",107,-34,1],["",11,-34,1],["",107,-34,1],["016105cf_16dfaf2b",11,-16,1,"please add `Include-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.mac:mac15-x64-rel-tests|browser_tests` to make sure this isn't causing problems for mac (where normally browser tests are skipped on the CQ)."],["8f0e1e17_abd81b49",107,-2,1,"Given the `GlobalBrowserCollection` now supports iteration in creation order we shouldn't need to use the `browser_tracker_` to support this behavior anymore - we can probably remove it at this point."],["d5c6b566_6ea007a2",107,-1,1,"nit: I think we should be able to remove these two includes."]],0,22],[7226255,20426,171,4.195,3.394,[[1,19]],[],0,23],[7089811,20429,37,1.326,1.047,[[2,4]],[["",8,-39,1],["",49,-39,0],["",108,-39,0],["",8,-37,1]],0,24],[7236591,20431,11,0.407,0.29,[[1,20]],[["c69a9e72_bfeda9eb",109,0,1,"nit: We may want to add more detail on when this is called exactly, something along the lines of what we have for `BrowserWindowFeatures::Init()`, i.e. ``` // Called exactly once to initialize…"]],0,25],[7244851,20432,36,1.326,1.047,[[2,5]],[],0,26],[7249650,20433,36,1.326,1.047,[[2,5]],[],0,26],[7254436,20436,6,0.248,0.178,[[1,21]],[],0,27],[7269944,20439,1,0.142,0.088,[[1,22]],[],0,28],[7280243,20445,11,0.407,0.29,[[1,23]],[],0,29],[7230065,20448,131,4.195,3.394,[[36,0.234,0,31],[4,0.22,2,29],[1,0.191,24,26],[11,0.156,4,21],[28,0.099,2,13],[2,0.064,6,7],[0,0.035,4,4]],[["0ff852cf_4cce6af8",110,-16,1,"nit: We can drop this param (the param defaults to kCreation which should be fine in this case)"],["371ce95d_c7cefa10",102,-16,1,"It looks like the only remaining client of `BrowserListEnumerator` is `browser_window_interface_iterator_non_android.cc`. I would avoid changing `BrowserListEnumerator` in this CL and perhaps we…"],["8b279376_60da8032",88,-16,1,"I think it's fine to leave usage of `BrowserList::begin()` and `BrowserList::end()` in browser_list.cc. It keeps the `BrowserList` implementation consistent (deals only with the list of browsers it…"],["9478d173_4d3f5077",1,-16,1,"We have tests that assert when a browser is closed / destroyed it is removed from the collection. Similar to the suggestion above I think it's fine to simply remove this check (`browser` is a…"],["ac8d2ebf_7dcf4cb0",111,-16,1,"I would consider dropping this check - or switching to `ASSERT_TRUE(GlobalBrowserCollection::GetInstance().empty());` since `browser()` should be a dangling ref at this point."],["cf5ed8e2_d389d520",112,-16,1,"nit: Similar to above - unless we explicitly need an order for the iteration I would suggest dropping this param (here and elsewhere further below)"],["ec9fdf03_c8da819b",20,-16,1,"`GlobalBrowserCollection::GetInstance()` can be assumed to always return a valid instance - we should be ok to remove this check"],["11f4ab92_8b50af62",113,-15,0,"if `browser` must no be null, can we use '&' as the parameter? (Note: beyond the scope of this CL, so splitting the work to follow up CLs should be fine)."],["59a6a96e_b0d34c38",113,-15,1,"nit: Similar to above, we can remove this param"],["62116a0f_6d2c7e6f",114,-15,1,"nit: We can remove this explicit param (the default should work fine here)"],["81c0694b_5008007a",115,-15,1,"nit: Also here"],["a6d4e565_5e0ee611",1,-15,1,"nit/clar: any equivalent condition we can keep checking?"],["cc14dd26_9c4ca15a",20,-15,1,"nit: Also here"],["f09db327_77f6356f",4,-15,1,"nit: We should be able to remove this forward declaration and the friend class below also."]],0,30]]}